# Which FIESTA node(s) this stack serves — comma-separated list of
# magic | kdd | cdr | karar | erda | osu-mgr | sc. One API (/v2/{node}/...), one
# worker and one frontend (http://localhost:8080/MagIC/, /KArAr/, ...) serve
# every listed node; infrastructure (Postgres/OpenSearch/RustFS/Mailpit) is
# shared. The portal bar links listed nodes locally, the rest to earthref.org.
# `make` targets also honor FIESTA_NODE overrides on the command line.
# `all` (also the default when unset or empty) is every node configurations/fiesta.yaml
# lists, so a new node needs no change here.
#   FIESTA_NODE=magic
#   FIESTA_NODE=magic,karar,cdr
FIESTA_NODE=all

# Uncomment to make `make up` (and down/ps/logs/build/infra) run the local
# API/SPA against that file's Postgres/OpenSearch/S3, as `make up ENV_FILE=…`
# does; `make up ENV_FILE=` then runs a local stack. init/user/rebuild/seed/
# fiesta still need ENV_FILE on the command line to touch the remote.
#   ENV_FILE=.env.prod

# How many of dev.earthref.org's most recent public contributions `make seed`
# imports into each node (default 50; 0 imports none). `make seed
# FIESTA_SEED_PUBLIC=10` overrides it once; `ARGS="--public N"` beats both.
#   FIESTA_SEED_PUBLIC=50

# Infrastructure secrets (change for anything beyond local dev).
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=fiesta
RUSTFS_ACCESS_KEY=fiesta
RUSTFS_SECRET_KEY=fiesta-secret
FIESTA_SECRET_KEY=dev-only-change-me

# Sign-in providers (optional; docs/api.md "Authentication"). Each is offered
# once both its values are set. Locally the redirect base must be set (the Vite
# proxy hides the public URL from the API); register
# <FIESTA_OAUTH_REDIRECT_BASE>/auth/oauth/<provider>/callback with each provider.
# Without them, sign in with an emailed link and read it in Mailpit (:8025).
# FIESTA_OAUTH_REDIRECT_BASE=http://localhost:8080/MagIC/v2
# FIESTA_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# FIESTA_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# FIESTA_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=
# FIESTA_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=
# FIESTA_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# FIESTA_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# FIESTA_ORCID_CLIENT_ID=
# FIESTA_ORCID_CLIENT_SECRET=
# FIESTA_ORCID_URL=https://sandbox.orcid.org

# Published host ports (override if something else is already listening).
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
OPENSEARCH_PORT=9200
RUSTFS_API_PORT=9000
RUSTFS_CONSOLE_PORT=9001
MAILPIT_WEB_PORT=8025
API_PORT=8000
FRONTEND_PORT=8080

# Use a distinct project and ports when running another checkout alongside this one.
#COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=fiesta-my-worktree
